/rivalry-week-live-cfp-takeaways","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 'College GameDay' Week 13: Duke vs. Wake Forest","description":"\"College GameDay\" heads to Wake Forest University for Week 13.","published":"2026-11-27T17:21:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50612493/2026-college-gameday-week-13-duke-vs-wake-forest","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"How every 2027 five-star college football prospect will fit","description":"There are 23 five-star players in the class, and we scout each one's game for the next level.","published":"2026-11-27T17:00:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/recruiting/story/_/id/48543549/college-football-recruiting-2027-prospects-five-star-scouts-take","type":"Story","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Which teams have the best odds to make the College Football Playoff?","description":"We are tracking the odds for making the CFP, earning a bye and winning it all.","published":"2026-11-27T15:51:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Houston, rivalry color rushes lead top uniforms of CFB Week 13","description":"Just because it's rivalry week doesn't mean teams still can't put their best foot forward with uniform swag.","published":"2026-11-27T15:00:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50598211/college-football-uniforms-week-13-houston","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What the world looked like the last time Texas A&M beat Texas","description":"It has been 15 years since Texas A&M came out on top on the gridiron against its rivals to the southwest.","published":"2026-11-27T17:36:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/47109982/texas-aggies-lone-star-showdown-last-win-2010","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft Big Board rankings: Mel Kiper's top 25 prospects, best by position","description":"Three quarterbacks who could go early? Big changes in the rankings? Mel Kiper Jr. stacks the best players on the 2027 draft board as of late November.","published":"2026-11-27T14:49:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50182998/2027-nfl-draft-rankings-kiper-big-board-top-prospects","type":"Story","byline":"Mel Kiper Jr.","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios in Week 13?","description":"Plenty of spots are still up for grabs entering the final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-27T12:39:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50583399/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-13","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5031157/reed-harris","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed_Harris_(American_football)"},"pick":{"pick":48,"round":2,"team":"NE","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Reed Harris (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed_Harris_(American_football)","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:14Z","intro":"Reed Harris is an American football wide receiver for the Arizona State Sun Devils. He previously played for the Boston College Eagles.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Harris was born in Minnesota, and moved to Conrad, Montana when he was a year old, growing up on a 12,000 acre farm. Harris moved to Great Falls, Montana when he was in 8th grade, later attending Great Falls High School where he was the football team's starting quarterback as a sophomore and junior. He moved to wide receiver during his senior season and finished with 553 yards and three touchdowns. Harris finished his high school career completing 229 passes for 21 touchdowns, while adding 1,575 yards and 13 touchdowns on the ground, with 36 receptions for 536 yards and four touchdowns through the air. He also added 83 tackles with ten being for a loss, nine sacks, five fumble recoveries, and a forced fumble on defense. Coming out of high school, Harris was rated as a three-star recruit in football, basketball, and track by 247Sports, and was ranked as the top player in the state of Montana in the class of 2023. He committed to play college football for the Boston College Eagles over offers from other schools such as Iowa State, Oregon State, Montana, Montana State, Colorado State, Utah State, San Diego State, Central Michigan, Harvard, Idaho, and Idaho State."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"BOSTON COLLEGE\nAs a freshman in 2023, Harris appeared in four games, making one catch, as he was redshirted. In week 2 of the 2024 season, he caught his first career touchdown in a win over Duquesne. During the 2024 season, Harris played in all 13 games with 11 starts, catching 17 passes for 486 yards and four touchdowns. During the 2025 season, he totaled 39 catches for 673 yards and five touchdowns; after the conclusion of the season, he entered the NCAA transfer portal."}]}}